One possible distinction here is that it's not possible or desirable
to keep every item you've discovered in your inventory and/or cache
(assuming you even have the latter), so if you get 'flayed you're
eventually going to run into un-IDd items for which you don't have in-
game notes.

My compromise is to write down, out of game, just what the scroll of
identify is. I write down significant level and altar locations too
but no other item IDs. Some may consider even this cheating; fine with
me. I haven't actually had to use the scroll of ID information in any
recent ascension, as since item IDs have been vulnerable to 'flayers I
generally genocide them first, and in a no-gen game never let them get
within melee range.

